Bryce - my recommendation =97 candidly, and not as legal advice =97 is to k=
eep the reseller structure we built. Here=92s why, taking your biggest conc=
ern first.


1. The indemnities are narrower than they read. Look at what =A78 actually =
triggers on: information accuracy, honest scope of work, disclosure of pre-=
existing issues, timely funding, and your representations to your client. F=
ive of the six are conduct-based =97 they only fire on something you or Sub=
contractorHub does or fails to do, and every one of them mirrors into the S=
MB template we provided, so the party that causes a problem is the party th=
at ultimately pays for it. You=92re not indemnifying us for our failures; t=
he annex sits on top of the MSSA=92s indemnities, which run both directions=
. The one genuinely broad piece =97 acts and omissions of the workers thems=
elves =97 is standard across the EOR industry, because you and your client =
direct their day-to-day work, not us. If your counsel has specific language=
 concerns there, send us the redlines and we=92ll run them through our team=
.


2. The risk you=92re solving for is exactly what the product absorbs. EOR e=
xists so that nobody in this chain =97 not you, not SubcontractorHub =97 is=
 the legal employer internationally. PrismHR employs the Bulgaria team, run=
s the compliance, and carries the employer obligations. Your role in the mi=
ddle is a conduit for terms, not a catch basin for risk.


3. The referral path costs your client real money on day one. The deposit w=
aiver you negotiated is a term of your agreement =97 it doesn=92t travel. I=
f we contract SubcontractorHub directly, our standard structure reinstates =
the refundable security deposit (about one month of each employee=92s full =
employment cost, per head, before start) plus the first-month prefund =97 r=
oughly two months of employment cost per employee in upfront cash that Subc=
ontractorHub doesn=92t owe today. Under your reseller agreement as written,=
 that stays waived.


4. And it costs you the position. Under reseller, you own the client relati=
onship, set your own price, and keep the margin =97 on this deal and every =
one behind it. Under referral, we contract your client directly and you ste=
p out of the middle. That solves the liability question by giving up the th=
ing that makes this yours. Structurally it=92s also a restart =97 new party=
, new paper, new terms =97 and the August payroll date doesn=92t survive it=
.


The clean path: keep the reseller agreement as established, send over any s=
pecific redlines your counsel wants considered, and let=92s sign inside the=
 current window so the Bulgaria team makes August payroll. Every concern yo=
u=92ve raised is addressable inside the structure you already have. The alt=
ernative addresses it by making the deal smaller for you and more expensive=
 for your client.


Standing by=85


Antaeus



